# Line endings.
#
# Before this file the repo had no policy, and the result was the worst
# possible split: 128 files LF, 14 CRLF, and the CRLF set was not some
# forgotten corner -- it held App.tsx, MapCanvas.tsx, mission/types.ts,
# features/registry.ts and RouteAnalysisInspector.tsx, which are the files
# everyone touches. mission/types.ts had at one point been left with a mix of
# both inside the same file.
#
# That produces conflicts on lines nobody edited: two people save the same
# untouched region with different endings and git sees every line as changed.
# It also makes real diffs unreadable, which is how a 15-line change once
# showed up as 1102.
#
# text=auto lets git decide what is text (it looks for NUL bytes, and already
# classifies all 48 binaries here correctly); eol=lf commits and checks out
# text as LF, matching the existing majority. The explicit binary lines below
# are belt and braces for the formats present -- a misclassified binary is
# silently corrupted by normalisation, and bsc5.bin in particular is a packed
# Float32 array full of bytes that would otherwise look like line endings.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.glb  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf  binary
*.zip  binary
*.bin  binary
*.tif  binary
*.tiff binary
*.npy  binary
*.mp4  binary
